NXEngine-evo @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=====================================================================

NXEngine-evo is the open-source engine of Cave Story (Doukutsu Monogatari,
Studio Pixel, 2004), the platform adventure. This is its AmigaOS 3.x build
for a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, with SDL 2 through GFOpenGPU. Status:
TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AmiCradle or an RTG board.
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/ from gfopenrtg's main of
  2 November 2026 or later (the game's own 320x240 screen), with
  SDL2_mixer.module and SDL2_image.module.
- AHI for sound. GFOpenInput for pads (lowlevel.library alone gives the
  joystick port).
- The Cave Story data (freeware, not in this archive): see below.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x nxengine-evo-...lha
Games:). Then the data, prepared on a PC with Python 3, git and tar, from
the port's repository:

    git clone https://github.com/DalsinAI/amiganxengine
    cd amiganxengine
    OUT=nxdata sh runtime-data/build-amiga.sh
    tar -xf nxdata/nx-data.tar -C <the NXEngine drawer>

That fetches the freeware Cave Story data from the address the repository
pins, checks its SHA-256, and lays it out with the engine's own data as
the game wants it (661 files in data/). Settings and saves go to the
drawer's User drawer, made on the first run.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the game's icon, or from a Shell: cd to the drawer, then
  nxengine-evo (-fps logs the frame rate to User/debug.log).
- The game starts on a 320x240 screen of its own; Options, Graphics
  changes it.
- Keys: the cursor keys move (Down examines, saves at a save disk), Z
  jumps and accepts, X fires, A and S change weapon, Q is the inventory,
  W the map, Escape the menu, F9 a screenshot (in User). Options,
  Controls changes them. A stick or CD32 pad in port 2: red jumps, blue
  fires, Play is the menu.
- Quit from the menu (Escape, Quit).

Licence
-------

NXEngine-evo is GPL-3.0 (LICENSE); its source is at
https://github.com/nxengine/nxengine-evo. Cave Story is freeware by
Studio Pixel under its own terms and is not part of this archive. The
icons are drawn from NXEngine-evo's own program icon.

